 "honest": [
  "The floor is a property of the TEST, not of the market: it says which effect sizes this panel size (17 cells x ~80 months, ~26 window months per cell) could have flagged at 80% power, and says nothing about whether a bigger effect exists.",
  "Power is computed for a multiplicative window effect that hits every cell in the same direction. An effect concentrated in a few cells, or pointing both ways, needs a bigger per-cell move to be detected -- the per-cell floors published here are that reading.",
  "The permuted null keeps the observed |gap| multisets, so the floor inherits this panel's own gap dispersion: a quieter panel would show a lower floor without the world being easier to read.",
  "Cells are a cross-section on the SAME timeline, so the pooled p counts correlated members as separate evidence -- the floor is published beside the per-cell floors for that reason."
 ],
